# Dedicated hosting onboarding

Before adding, enabling, or materially changing dedicated hosting, read
`docs/dedicated-server-game-checklist.md` and `docs/server-hosting-parity-plan.md`.

Apply the checklist to community, customer-owned, party-dedicated and self-hosted
games, including editions and shared-installation aliases. Do not claim all-game
support because a feature works on one Steam game or one operating system.

Use existing recipes, ServerControlAdapter, typed settings, public Join flow,
party permissions, and the single Ctrl+P helper. Record verified controls and
explicit engine limitations. Never treat an unknown player count as empty.

Catalog edits still follow `platform/AGENTS.md` and the browser/admin workflow.
Do not pull secrets, edit environment files, or overwrite unrelated database data.
